34,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some really important stuff! It turns out that if someone cancels late for a whole-building let, the rest of us have to cover their cost. That's not fair at all!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,That does sound like a difficult situation for those who stay. It is important that no one feels burdened by others' absences. I wonder if we can find a way to make the camp more inviting.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The administrative burden is a serious concern. Public bookings require a tedious lottery and a rigid application process that is incredibly time-consuming to correct. We must consider options that don't exhaust the organizers before the camp even begins.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Eight people to a room with a strict lights-out? That sounds like a crowded nightmare! If we're all squeezed in like sardines, nobody's going to sleep well, and we'll all be grumpy again!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The transport costs vary wildly depending on the distance. If we go too far, the travel expenses alone could easily blow our budget and leave us in a deficit again.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Exactly! And since transport is such a huge part of the cost, we have to be careful. If we pick a far place and people drop out, the price for everyone else will skyrocket!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is a worry indeed. I noticed that some members have not attended in the past, and some even left the club shortly after. Perhaps if we choose a place that fosters connection, more will want to join.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Beyond the paperwork, we must consider the daily labor. Last year, the cooking duty took two hours every day. If we choose a place without catering, we are simply shifting the burden onto the organizers.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, if the public beds are only 1,100 yen, that's super cheap! But if it means sleeping eight people to a room, it's not worth it. We need a place where we can actually relax!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"We can't just look at the base price. Between the non-refundable deposits for building lets and the volatile transport costs, a ""cheap"" option can quickly become a financial risk for the club.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I totally agree with Misaki! We can't just look at the sticker price. If we want it to be fair, we need a plan for those late cancellations so the remaining members aren't stuck paying extra!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,Perhaps we should consider a place where we all stay together in one building. The seniors mentioned that the evenings are when the different year-groups truly begin to bond and speak with one another.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Staying in one building is fine, but not if it requires a nine-page application and a lottery. We must prioritize a destination with professional catering and a simple booking process to avoid organizer burnout.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we're all in one building and it's too crowded, we'll just be fighting over space! We need a place that's cozy but not ""sardine-style,"" or we'll be too tired to bond!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we prioritize bonding and comfort over the lowest possible price, we must be realistic about the funding. We cannot afford another year where the club account covers the shortfall.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm with you, Misaki! Let's find a place that's comfortable and easy to book, but we absolutely have to agree on a fair way to handle the costs and cancellations first!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I understand your concerns. Perhaps we can find a balance where the booking is simple and the cost is fair, yet the layout encourages us to spend quality time together as a whole club.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We must be realistic. If we choose a destination that requires extensive manual labor or bureaucratic hurdles, the organizers will be too exhausted to actually train. Professional catering and streamlined booking are non-negotiable for a sustainable camp.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I agree with Ryuji about the catering! If we're not exhausted from cooking and we have actual space to sleep, we'll have way more energy for the adventure part! Let's pick somewhere comfy!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"Then we should prioritize a local destination with professional catering. It minimizes transport risks, avoids the lottery stress, and ensures we don't end up with a deficit that the club account has to cover.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
