58,3,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Campus Intensive seems safest for the budget! If we stay local, we won't have those huge transport costs or the risk of paying for people who cancel. It's the fairest way to make sure no one gets stuck with a huge bill!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"While the campus is convenient, I worry it may not provide the special atmosphere we need. To truly bridge the gap between year-groups, I believe we need a place where we all live together.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option B is out. The municipal system's lottery and rigid application process are far too demanding. We cannot risk the organizers spending their entire month on paperwork and then being exhausted before the camp even starts.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option B is definitely a no! Eight people to a room and a strict lights-out? We'll be zombies! I want something exciting, but we need to actually sleep so we can have fun!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option C is too risky. The distance would make transport costs unpredictable, and the non-refundable deposit for a whole building could leave the club account in a deficit if people cancel. Option A is the only financially sound choice.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"I get that Shizue wants a special atmosphere, but is it worth the risk? If we go with Option A, we can spend the money we save on transport on something really fun for everyone instead!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"That is a lovely thought, Mio. However, I fear that staying on campus may feel too much like a normal school day. To truly bond, we need a shared space away from our daily routines.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"If we prioritize the organizers' well-being, Option C is the most logical. It provides professional catering and a straightforward booking process, avoiding both the bureaucratic nightmare of Option B and the labor of Option A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Option C sounds like a real adventure! It's a whole building just for us, and we won't be squeezed in like sardines. Plus, with the owner doing the meals, we can actually relax!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"Professional catering is a plus, but the distance is the problem. Two prefectures away means transport will be the biggest expense. We cannot gamble with the club's funds on a destination we've never used.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"But if we go with Option C, we're back to that non-refundable deposit problem! If someone drops out, the rest of us pay. That's just not fair. I'm voting for Option A to keep it fair for everyone!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I understand the financial worries, but we must not forget the members who feel disconnected. A shared home at the Coastal Lodge could be the key to bringing our fragmented year-groups back together. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,Option A is not a solution; it simply shifts the burden of accommodation and meals back onto the members or organizers. Option C is the only choice that ensures the organizers can actually train. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm voting for Option C too! It's a real adventure, we get our own building, and we won't be exhausted from cooking or crowded rooms. Let's go to the coast and actually have some fun!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I cannot support Option C. The financial risk is too high, and we cannot afford another deficit. For the stability of the club's accounts and the fairness of the fees, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I really wanted a fun adventure, but I can't ignore the risk of unfair costs. I'll stick with Option A to make sure no one gets stuck with a surprise bill!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It is a difficult choice, as I care deeply for both our finances and our friendships. However, for the sake of the club's heart and unity, I will remain with Option C.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The decision is clear. Option A fails to address the labor burden, and Option B is a bureaucratic disaster. Option C is the only choice that protects the organizers' time and health. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm sticking with Option C! It's the only one that sounds like a real trip and won't leave us all grumpy and tired. Let's go to the beach and have the best camp ever!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I've tried to warn everyone about the financial risks, but the majority prefers the lodge. I'll vote for Option A one last time to prioritize the budget, but I'll help manage the costs if C is chosen.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
